    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.chunk }}",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "OCR cleanup filter. Input: one chunk raw Mistral OCR markdown. Output: same text, noise stripped. Nothing else.\n\nRULES\nFilter, not editor. No summarize, rephrase, translate, improve.\nRetained text = byte-identical to input.\nNo commentary, no preamble, no code fences.\nNo truncation. Process to last line.\nAmbiguous? KEEP. False deletion worse than leftover noise.\n\nREMOVE\nPage numbers: bare digits, \"Page 3\", \"- 12 -\", \"3/47\", 第 5 页\nRunning headers/footers: short lines repeating title / org / doc ID\nWatermarks: DRAFT, CONFIDENTIAL, COPY, 样本, scanner banners\nArtifacts: stray glyphs (| ~ ^ ¬ ° ■ ●) alone or at line edges; separator runs (--- ___ ...) not markdown\nScan furniture: \"Scanned by...\", confidence notes, caption-less ![img-0.jpeg](img-0.jpeg)\nHyphenation across linebreak: \"govern-\\nment\" -> \"government\". Latin only. Never touch CJK chars.\n\nKEEP EXACT\nBody text, original order\nMarkers: 第X条, 第X章, Article X, §, numbered/lettered clauses\nMarkdown tables, whole, pipes and alignment rows\nReal headings (document structure, not page furniture)\nBlank lines between blocks\nCJK punctuation, full-width chars\n\nEDGES\nNumber fused to body (\"...shall apply. 12 Article 5\") -> delete number only, keep both sides.\nHeader = real title on page 1 -> keep first occurrence, drop repeats.\nChunk starts/ends mid-sentence -> emit fragment as-is. Do not complete. Do not flag.\n\nOutput cleaned chunk. Nothing else."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "n-clean",
      "name": "Clean Chunk",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.5,
